  "platform_acceptance_groups": [
    "Real development users authenticate with Authorization Code + PKCE; admin-only estate creation and assigned manager scope",
    "Two divisions, ten unique rubber blocks with clone/planting/tree metadata; create/read/update, persisted relationships and domain rejection",
    "All four Estate lifecycle event types are atomic, confirmed, contract-valid and projected with canonical IDs using bounded polling",
    "Canonical-UUID GeoJSON import: estate + two divisions + ten nonoverlapping WGS84 polygons, validity/SRID and spheroidal hectares",
    "Gateway spatial queries retrieve estate boundary, all block geometry, point membership, bbox/centroids, GIS layers and GeoJSON export",
    "Actual Spatial v1 envelopes validate and confirmed publications reach the durable diagnostic queue",
    "VIEWER cannot modify boundary; unassigned users cannot read/write/import; database roles cannot connect across ownership boundaries",
    "Direct backend JWT/estate authorization without gateway, 2 MiB request limits and authenticated runtime OpenAPI contracts",
    "RabbitMQ duplicates and out-of-order revisions are idempotent; parent-late child snapshots are retained and reconcile when the estate arrives",
    "Durable W3C HTTP -> transactional outbox -> RabbitMQ publish -> Spatial consume spans are visible together in Jaeger",
    "Spatial serves existing geometry and layers while Estate is stopped; safe gateway 503 and independent restart recovery",
    "Broker outage preserves pending atomic outbox; messaging resumes without duplicate projection effects"
  ],
